name "Redstone signals"

every redstone pulse do
    input from a
    output to b
end

every 20 ticks do
    -- Label a lever, comparator, redstone block, or other signal source "abc".
    -- Connect it to this manager's cable network and push the labels.
    -- With no side specified, read its strongest emitted signal (0-15).
    if abc has gt 0 redstone:: then
        input from a
        output to b
    end
end

every 20 ticks do
    -- A side reads the signal emitted through that face of the labeled block.
    if abc east side has ge 8 redstone:: then
        input from a
        output to b
    end
end

-- Labeled queries read emitted signals, not incoming neighbor power.
-- Readings update when the source changes. Reading does not consume redstone.
-- redstone:: reads signal strength on world sources and stored units in buffers.
-- The redstone item is a different resource. World signals remain read-only.
-- Experimental buffers transfer stored units and expose them to comparators.
-- See "Buffer redstone counter (experimental)" for a counter example.
-- Use SOME/EVERY to query multiple labeled sources individually:
-- IF SOME abc HAS GT 0 redstone:: THEN ... END
-- OVERALL adds their strengths; EACH SIDE also adds the selected face readings,
-- including NULL's strongest-face reading. Omit sides to read each block once.

every 20 ticks do
    -- this checks the redstone signal on the manager block
    if redstone ge 2 then
        input from a
        output to b
    end
end
